Moreover, even high-powered experiments can yield completely uninformative results (Wagenmakers, Verhagen, & Ly, 2016). Consider Study 6 from Donnellan, Lucas, and Cesario (2015), one of nine replication attempts on the reported phenomenon that lonely people take hotter showers (in order to replace the lack of social warmth with physical warmth; Bargh & Shalev, 2012). Although the overall results provided compelling evidence in favor of the null hypothesis (Wagenmakers, Verhagen, & Ly, 2016), three of the nine studies by Donnellan et al. (2015) produced only weak evidence for \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
